From 2f8ffb21d0a385c6dca3dee67f321b894a9b1157 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrea Campanella <emuboy85@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 21:35:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: PS2: Add the Graphics Synthesizer device /dev/ps2gs for
 programs

A program maps a packet buffer and the driver sends GIF and VIF1 packets
with the DMA controller. The driver waits for the DMA end and for the
vertical sync with interrupts, with polling as the fallback. It gives
access to the display registers (PMODE, DISPFB, DISPLAY, BGCOLOR) and
restores them when the program stops.

The design follows the ps2gs and ps2dma drivers of the Sony PlayStation 2
Linux kit.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [meta-playstation2 specific, not sent to the fork yet]
